{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the market is in a downtrend (prices falling from ~65 to ~52), failing to capture the magnitude of the decline.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion lag: The model reacts too slowly to price drops, predicting a slow recovery or stabilization while the true market bottoms out and begins a volatile rebound; adjust forecasts downward immediately upon detecting a multi-day decline.",
    "Ignore positive sentiment signals during downtrends: Positive sentiment scores (0.20) in the history do not correlate with price increases in this period; treat sentiment as noise during strong bearish momentum.",
    "Adjust for overshoot on recovery: The model underestimates the speed and height of the price rebound (recovery from ~52 to ~60); increase forecast slope during the recovery phase to match the observed volatility.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: For the first 10 days of the forecast horizon, apply a fixed downward adjustment of 3-5 EUR to align with the immediate downtrend; for days 11-30, apply a convex upward adjustment to anticipate the rebound."
  ]
}
